Echo Chamber...\

\b0 This brings up a panel which lets you perform recursive echos throughout a sound.  The mechanism is highly volatile and requires careful tweaking to get good results, but it does work.  I threw it together one day and include it here only because it's interesting to play with, especially for getting weird inside-a-metal-box echos.\
\
The parameters are:\
\

\pard\tx2180\tx2660\tx3200\tx3720\tx4260\tx4800\tx5320\tx5780\tx7560\tx8980\b\fi-1640\li2180\fc1\cf1 Ratio	
\b0 The amplitude of the echos generated, expressed as a fraction of the original sound.
\b \
First Delay	
\b0 The number of seconds after a sound before the first echo is produced
\b \
Delay	
\b0 The number of seconds between each subsequent echo
\b \
Dropoff	
\b0 The amplitude of echo 
\i n+1
\i0  as a percentage of the amplitude of echo 
\i n.
\b\i0 \
Initial	
\b0 The amplitude of the first echo as a percentage of the amplitude of the original sound.\

